: significant risk of serious injury above the diaphragm</article-title><source>Injury</source><year>1992</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1618570</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0020-1383(05)80013-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chowaniec</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobek</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jablonski</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kabiesz-Nenickza</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Karczewska</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Case-study from fatal gunshot wounds from non-lethal projectiles</article-title><source>Forensic Sci Int</source><year>2008</year><volume>178</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>217</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18514453</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.forsciint.2008.03.020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ritchie</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibbons</surname><given-names>JRP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Plastic bullets in Northern Ireland</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1990</year><volume>301</volume><fpage>1332</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2271867</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.301.6764.1332</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Voiglio</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fanton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Caillot</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Neidhardt</surname><given-names>JPH</given-names></name><name><surname>Malicier</surname><given-names>D</given-names></